# ---------------- Arcade_Spawner.events (Task 7 Part G3: refill the lane) ----------------
# Every three seconds, while the player is close enough, put one more enemy on the floor ahead.
# `EnemiesAlive` is a global the enemy sheet decrements on death, so the lane cannot swamp.
#
# `me is near player by 60` works as a CONDITION here (a `when every` line plus a gate), which is
# what makes the spawner repeat instead of firing once on the `near` enter-edge. Lowercase
# `player` resolves to the nearest player in conditions too, so the sheet keeps working if the
# scene names the hero something else.
#
# SETUP (editor): the scene's `Arcade_Spawner` actor carries an EventSheet with Event File =
# Arcade_Spawner; `SpawnAhead` is an EmptyActor where the clones appear.

# Zeroed once per play session, so the first `add 1 to EnemiesAlive` reads a real value instead
# of an unset global (which reads 0 and warns once).
when me appears
  set EnemiesAlive to 0

when every 3 seconds
  me is near player by 200
  unless EnemiesAlive is higher than 3
  add 1 to EnemiesAlive
  spawn Arcade_Enemy at SpawnAhead
  print "Spawner: one more enemy ahead"
